ntime", "call_id": "toolu_014AfzjtWFX4ztMXcbuWYidK", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 157236, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014AfzjtWFX4ztMXcbuWYidK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 161134, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LpDsamEPzU5WZJ9oremSA9", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "After this morning's payments-worker v3.4.0 deploy, the service became unhealthy with an 18% error rate. payments-api (v5.1.0) also showed errors (18%), but the user confirmed those come from the worker. payments-worker was rolled back in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm payments-worker and payments-api have recovered, then find the root cause in v3.4.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 161734, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LpDsamEPzU5WZJ9oremSA9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 161734, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LpDsamEPzU5WZJ9oremSA9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 164325, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NFmfUSEAx8d4mi4zt72cu7", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 164625, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NFmfUSEAx8d4mi4zt72cu7", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 164625, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NFmfUSEAx8d4mi4zt72cu7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 164625, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Q5U9GPNiiSiSvmctHS23PP", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 164925, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Q5U9GPNiiSiSvmctHS23PP", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 164925, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Q5U9GPNiiSiSvmctHS23PP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 170735, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still showing errors.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Identified the service:** There's no service called \"payments.\" I found two unhealthy payments services, both at an 18% error rate: payments-worker on v3.4.0 and payments-api on v5.1.0. You confirmed the worker was the one affected by this morning's deploy and that the API errors come from it.\n- **Rolled back payments-worker:** It's now on v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production, in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It reports healthy, and its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%. No approval was needed because v3.3.0 was already healthy in production.\n- **Opened the incident:** SEV2 **INC-0001** is open for payments-worker, and on-call has been paged.\n\n**Still broken: payments-api.** Right after the rollback it was still unhealthy at 18% errors. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. But its current version, v5.1.0, is itself listed as \"degraded\" in its release history, so it may have its own problem. Its last healthy release was v5.0.0. I didn't roll it back because you said only the worker was affected. If the API doesn't recover soon, rolling it back to v5.0.0 is the obvious next step. Just say if you want me to do that.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PJFgWMJiqdp3kwkJPdsvmp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012jvVoN1vu9FszmEnbZz6Lw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014XnVcjgDBp23c6SznQ89oD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JKdiEeZVW4ycrdpHZ3R1hk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Pt7M9Qvo1RckXZdPyaXtCy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013neLFF6oAvGhrtLyzuSnYH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016jTyYjRT4jbRz1rJGNVCNB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014NCYKU58Kn7cy9agMHhcsM", "caller": {"